From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] xinput: Don't wait for the update thread while holding the loader lock.

The first XInput call starts the HID update thread and waits for it to
enumerate controllers. A new thread can't start while the calling thread
holds the loader lock, so that wait never ends.

FlatOut 2 calls SteamAPI_Init() with the loader lock held. GE's lsteamclient
Sony controller fallback queries XInput during Steam Input setup, so the
game froze at startup. Its log shows a new thread waiting on loader_section,
blocked by the main thread, right after steamclient initialised.
PROTON_SONY_AUTO_XINPUT=0, which turns that fallback off, works around it.

Skip the wait when the loader lock is held. The update thread runs once the
lock is released and finds the controllers then. Calls made without the
loader lock still wait as before.

https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/issues/939
---
--- a/dlls/xinput1_3/main.c
+++ b/dlls/xinput1_3/main.c
@@ -1181,7 +1181,15 @@
     if (!thread) ERR("failed to create update thread, error %lu\n", GetLastError());
     CloseHandle(thread);
 
-    WaitForSingleObject(start_event, INFINITE);
+    /* A new thread can't start while this thread holds the loader lock, so
+     * waiting for it here deadlocks. That happens when a game calls
+     * SteamAPI_Init() with the loader lock held and lsteamclient's
+     * controller fallback queries XInput. The update thread finds the
+     * controllers once the loader lock is released. */
+    if (RtlIsCriticalSectionLockedByThread(NtCurrentTeb()->Peb->LoaderLock))
+        WARN("loader lock held, not waiting for the update thread\n");
+    else
+        WaitForSingleObject(start_event, INFINITE);
     return TRUE;
 }
 
